{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]High on a mountain top what do I see?
[A]Bear tracks, bear tracks [D]lookin' back at [A]me
[A]Better get your rifles, boy, before it's too late
[A]The bear's got a little pig, and he's [D]headed through the [A]gate
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Well, he's [E]big around the middle and he's [A]broad across the rump
He's going [E]ninety miles an hour, takin' [A]thirty feet a jump
[A]He ain’t never been caught, he ain’t never been treed
[A]Some folks say he's a [D]lot like [A]me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I saved up my money and bought me some bees
And they started making honey way up in the trees
Cut down my tree and my honey's all gone
Ol' Slewfoots done made himself at home
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Winter's coming on and it's twenty below
And the rivers froze over, so where can he go?
We'll chase him up the gully and run him in a well,
And shoot him in the bottom just to listen to him yell
{end_of_chorus}
